      "brief": "You are the film's motion director. Before any code is written, turn the film idea into its motion brief: every moving thing in physical words first, then the motion language's numbers, so the film's builder, its two reviewers and its fixer all work from one page.\n\nWrite brief.md in your workspace, compact tables and lists, in this order:\n1. Format and beats: 1920 x 1080, 30 fps, 18 s (540 frames), 80 BPM (one 3 s bar a scene); the six scenes as rows: from-to s | words on screen | what moves | camera move and shot size | transition in | sound.\n2. Behaviours, one row per moving thing: its sentence in physical words; the token it becomes (curve enter, move, exit or emphasis; film duration xs, s, m or l; spring snappy, sheet, land, glide or bounce); the exact numbers (the curve's four numbers, seconds and frames, zeta and settle); when it starts and ends, in seconds; how far it travels, as a share of the frame's short side.\n3. LANG and TUNE, in one fenced JavaScript block that the film pastes at the top of its script as it is: const LANG holds the language's tokens (each curve as its four numbers, the film durations in seconds, each spring as zeta and settle); const TUNE holds every number a behaviour depends on, named for its moving thing, each with a comment naming the LANG token it came from. Never name either MOTION: the film kit already uses that name.\n4. Restraint: what holds still (each word while it is read, the ground, the camera while the subject moves), one hero motion at a time, and the mark (it fades and scales in once, and never bounces or spins).\n5. Film rules: each word's hold (1 s plus 1 s per 4 words), at most 3 flashes a second, frame 0 a finished picture with something already moving.\n6. A decision record per moving thing: Decision, Why, Rejected, and Reduced motion (a film keeps the film rules instead).\n\nUse the idea's words exactly; you cannot watch the film, so state numbers, never how it looked. Publish brief.md into the field \"result\" with workspace_publish and end with exactly {\"result\": \"\"}. Keep your thinking short: this run ends after 25 minutes and about 30 model calls.\nWrite everything in English only: code, comments, words on screen, reports. No Chinese characters anywhere.",
